{
  "title": "Insulin: response and supply",
  "sources": "5:26,28,30N",
  "stages": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "title": "Insulin resistance",
      "text": "Chapter five. Obesity is a risk factor for type two diabetes, but the connection is more than a label. The supplied notes describe insulin resistance: cells have difficulty using the insulin present."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.06,
      "title": "Supply contrast",
      "text": "Watch the tissue response weaken while insulin remains available. Contrast this with type one diabetes, where autoimmune destruction reduces the pancreatic beta-cell supply."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.28,
      "title": "Modifiable risk",
      "text": "Family history also changes risk. Exercise and weight management address modifiable contributors; they do not erase inherited susceptibility."
    }
  ],
